1934: # ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- review panel (-Panel)
1935: #
1936: # The roster is walked like the single-reviewer walk, without stopping at the first available
1937: # entry (Select-PanelMembers). Each member then runs as a complete consultation of its own - a
1938: # child run of this script (-PanelSpec) in a process of its own: own preflight, own recovery
1939: # record .consult.pending-<NN>.json, own parent thread (the newest of its lineage, or a new one;
1940: # -Mode new: new for all), own consultation id, handoff files
1941: # handoffs/NN-<engine>-<ReplyName>-<provider>.md and ledger entry with the `panel` record.
1942: # 0.4.x wave 21 (ROADMAP R11) - the members run IN PARALLEL; this run:
1943: #   1. takes the task lock (.consult.lock; its informational record names the panel) and holds
1944: #      it until the summary is printed: no other consultation or status update of the task in
1945: #      between (D12);
1946: #   2. judges EVERY recovery record of the task first: an active one refuses the panel, the
1947: #      inactive ones are consumed (numbering skips past them; D5);
1948: #   3. assigns n and NN to every member up front, in seat order (wave 26: panel.routing.picked -
1949: #      the roster order unless the panel is routed; member k: n0 + k - 1, NN0 + k - 1), so the
1950: #      files and the ledger keep that order whatever finishes first;
1951: #   4. writes every member's `reserved` record (the panel, n, NN, this process as writer and
1952: #      parent) BEFORE it launches any member - a member proves its parent with it, rewrites it
1953: #      with its own pid and only then checks that the parent lives (D6, D1, F07-1);
1954: #   5. launches the members as processes of their own (Start-Process; console output to files
1955: #      in a temp directory) along the plan of Get-PanelPlan - members of different endpoints at
1956: #      once, of one endpoint one after another unless the roster's "parallel" raises it,
1957: #      -PanelConcurrency caps the total (D8) - polls them, prints one line per finished member
1958: #      and stops a member that outlives its guard (its timeout + its format-repair and
1959: #      denial-retry budgets + (wave 24) its timeout continuation's -ContinueSec + 60 s write
1960: #      lock + 120 s, D11; Get-PanelMemberGuard);
1961: #   6. prints every member's console output in roster order, the summary with the panel's wall
1962: #      clock, and removes the records of members that never started anything (D5).
1963: # A member that fails or is refused does not stop the others; with -PanelConcurrency 1 a member
1964: # that leaves surviving processes stops the rest (recorded as skipped, exit 1; F15-3). Exit 0
1965: # only when every member produced a usable reply (-DryRun: when every member's plan could be
1966: # made; a dry run writes nothing and takes no lock).
