1360: # every other engine). Right before the start the engine's launch invariant is read afresh
1361: # (Get-EngineLaunchBlock -Fresh, D4 - muse: the billing guard re-reads auth.json and the
1362: # environment, never a sign-in cached by the preflight minutes earlier) and, for an engine other
1363: # than codex, the %-hazard of a .cmd launcher (F02-14); a refusal starts nothing. { Proc ($null
1364: # when nothing was started); Refusal ('' or why the launch was refused); Error ('' or why
1365: # Start-Process failed) }. Reads the run's $engineName and $repoRoot.
1366: function Start-EngineProcess {
1367:     param([string]$Launcher, [string[]]$Argv, [string]$StdoutPath, [string]$StderrPath, [string]$StdinPath)
1368:     $r = [pscustomobject]@{ Proc = $null; Refusal = ''; Error = '' }
